course: dictionary
lesson: 14453
title: Paramount: the most important thing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell us what matters most. Paramount is a formal word that means more important than anything else. «Safety is paramount» means that keeping people safe comes before everything else.
explain: Look at the clues around it. In «Children's welfare is paramount», the word welfare means health and happiness, so the sentence tells us that children's health and happiness must come first, above all else.
explain: You can check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «Safety is the most important thing» in place of «Safety is paramount». If it still makes sense, your meaning is right.
explain: Paramount is an adjective, so it describes a noun, like a paramount rule or a paramount concern. Formal writing, such as school rules and safety notices, uses it often.
fact: Paramount is an adjective, and it means more important than anything else.
fact: «Safety is paramount» means safety comes before everything else.
fact: Paramount is a formal word, so you will mostly find it in serious writing such as rules, reports and safety notices.
fact: A word with a similar meaning is «most important», but paramount sounds more serious and formal.
exercise: «The doctor said that patients' safety was paramount.» What does paramount mean here? | Very quiet | Less important than the rest | *More important than anything else | Easy to forget
exercise: Which swap keeps the meaning of «Safety is paramount»? | *Safety is the most important thing | Safety is forgotten | Safety is a long walk | Safety is a hobby
exercise: Find and copy the word that means more important than anything else. | *paramount | notice | safety | gate
test: «Our school's first rule is that kindness is paramount.» Paramount here means | Hardly anything | Just a little bit | *Most important of all | Something to forget
test: Which sentence uses paramount correctly? | The cake was paramount to the party | *The teacher said honesty is paramount in our class | The sky was paramount | My shoes are paramount, so I wore them
exam: Ella says paramount is a fancy way of saying "quite important". Is she right? | Yes, it means quite important | *No, it means more important than anything else | Yes, it means very quiet | No, it means happy
